/-!
# The presentation of the Fischer group `Fi₂₂` holds in its permutation model

The presentation selected for `Fi₂₂` is the ATLAS presentation on the standard generators, an
involution `a` and an element `b` of order `13` whose product has order `11`, with thirteen
relators (`TauCeti.Sporadic.fi22Presentation`). The generators `Fi22.a` and `Fi22.b` of the
degree-3510 model `TauCeti.Sporadic.Fi22` both have order `13`, so they are not such a pair. This
file gives two permutations `Fi22.imageA` and `Fi22.imageB` of the `3510` points, of orders `2`
and `13` with product of order `11`, that satisfy all thirteen relators and generate exactly the
model `Fi22`, and deduces that the presented group `SporadicName.Fi22.Group` maps onto the model.
In particular the presented group is nontrivial.

Each image is given by its table of images, so that the relators compute directly. Both are also
written as words in the generators of the model (`Fi22.imageA_eq`, `Fi22.imageB_eq`), which puts
them in the model; conversely `Fi22.a_eq` and `Fi22.b_eq` write the two generators of the model as
words in the two images, so the images generate the whole model.

The two permutations were found by a computer search in the model: a random involution with `694`
fixed points and random conjugates of the powers of `Fi22.a` and `Fi22.b` were tried until the
product had order `11` and the relators held, and the four words come from a search in the Cayley
graphs. Nothing about that search is used: the relators and both directions of generation are
checked here. Products follow Mathlib's convention `(σ * τ) x = σ (τ x)`, and it is in this
convention that the relators are evaluated.

No order of the model or of the presented group is asserted here, and the surjection is not shown
to be injective.

The lift and range arguments use `GroupPresentation.homEquiv` and
`GroupPresentation.exists_surjective_of_closure_range_eq`.

## Main declarations

* `TauCeti.Sporadic.Fi22.imageA`, `TauCeti.Sporadic.Fi22.imageB`: the images of the two
  generators, with `TauCeti.Sporadic.Fi22.presentationImage` the resulting assignment.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.Fi22.orderOf_imageA`, `TauCeti.Sporadic.Fi22.orderOf_imageB`,
  `TauCeti.Sporadic.Fi22.orderOf_imageA_mul_imageB`: the orders `2`, `13` and `11`.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.Fi22.lift_presentationImage_toFreeGroup_eq_one`: the thirteen relators hold.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.Fi22.closure_range_presentationImage`: the images generate the model.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.Fi22.presentationHom`, `TauCeti.Sporadic.Fi22.range_presentationHom`: the
  homomorphism from the presented group and its range.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.exists_surjective_Fi22`: the presented group maps onto the model.

## References

* R. A. Wilson, R. A. Parker, J. N. Bray et al., *ATLAS of Finite Group Representations*,
  version 3, presentation `F22G1-P1`,
  <https://brauer.maths.qmul.ac.uk/Atlas/v3/pres/F22G1-P1>.
* KitaKen1 (Kenta), *FiniteSimpleGroups*, `Fi22` construction at commit
  `7f09e33a9ceef6b59ce03e34cd4f0558c763e325`,
  <https://github.com/KitaKen1/finite-simple-groups-lean>, for the model in whose point numbering
  the images are given.
-/

