/-! ### Images of the standard generators -/

/- Each image is given by the table of its images, packed as in the model file: 117 hexadecimal
rows of 30 entries of three digits, the entry of the point `30 * r + j` being the group of three
digits of row `r` in position `j` counted from the right, read as field `30 * r + j` of width `12`
of the natural number having the rows as its digits in base `2 ^ 360`. The first image is an
involution, so its table is also the table of its preimages; the second image has a separate table
of preimages. The involution is built from its two inverse laws and not from
`Function.Involutive.toPerm`: the kernel decides `Function.LeftInverse` on `Fin 3510` through the
`Fintype` instance, whereas deciding the unfolded statement of `Function.Involutive` there exceeds
its recursion depth. The bodies are exposed so that importing modules can compute with the two
permutations. -/

/-- The image of the generator `a` of the presentation of `Fi₂₂`, of index zero: an involution of
the `3510` points. Entry `i` of the table is the image of the point `i`, and also its preimage. -/
